{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '103,122p' src/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd; sed -n '267,285p' src/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd; sed -n '1,50p' src/cljd/dao/stream/datagram/dart.cljd\"","aggregated_output":"\n\n(defn- wire!\n  \"Install the sole subscription on one dart:io WebSocket.\"\n  ([socket adapter] (wire! socket adapter nil))\n  ([socket adapter on-done]\n   (let [socket ^io/WebSocket socket]\n     (.listen socket\n              (fn [value]\n                (if (string? value)\n                  ((:message! adapter) value)\n                  ((:binary! adapter) value)))\n              .onError (fn [_error] ((:error! adapter)))\n              .onDone (fn []\n                        ((:closed! adapter)\n                         (or (.-closeCode socket) 1006)\n                         (or (.-closeReason socket) \"\"))\n                        (when on-done (on-done)))))\n   socket))\n\n        connections (atom #{})\n        config (assoc config :ws.dart/connections connections)\n        bind-future ^async/Future (io/HttpServer.bind bind-host bind-port)]\n    (-> bind-future\n        (.then (fn [server]\n                 (let [server ^io/HttpServer server]\n                   (reset! server-ref server)\n                   (.listen server\n                            (fn [request] (handle-request! config request))\n                            .onError\n                            (fn [_error]\n                              (deposit! :listener-error\n                                        (plain-error\n                                          :yin.repl.endpoint/listener-error\n                                          \"the host listener reported an error\"))))\n                   (deposit! :bind-succeeded\n                             {:host (.-address (.-address server))\n                              :port (.-port server)}))))\n        (.catchError\n(ns dao.stream.datagram.dart\n  \"The dart:io host seam of docs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md 3: one\n   RawDatagramSocket, bound once, whose read events deposit every received\n   datagram on the composition's deposit writer as plain\n   dao.stream.datagram values. The seam takes {:identity id :deposit w\n   :bind-host h :bind-port p :max-bytes n} -- a deposit writer and nothing\n   else, no function to invoke -- and returns at once {:send! f :close!\n   f}; binding is asynchronous here, so the bound event arrives when the\n   bind Future completes and a failed bind is deposited as bind-failed\n   from its error. The max-bytes drop is protocol validation below the\n   transform: never deposited. This adapter creates no timer and\n   schedules nothing; the composition drives every read of what it\n   deposits.\"\n  (:require [\"dart:io\" :as io]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.datagram :as datagram])\n  (:import [\"dart:typed_data\" Uint8List]))\n\n\n(defn- deposit-event!\n  \"One event onto the composition's deposit writer, total even if the\n   composition behind it is broken.\"\n  [deposit event]\n  (try (stream/append! deposit event)\n       (catch Object _ nil)))\n\n\n(defn- receive!\n  \"The socket's read transform: one deposited datagram event per datagram\n   the socket hands over, sourced from the address it observed, dropped\n   over the budget. It judges no datagram and invokes nothing above\n   itself.\"\n  [deposit identity max-bytes socket]\n  (when-some [^io/Datagram datagram (.receive ^io/RawDatagramSocket socket)]\n    (when (<= (.-length ^Uint8List (.-data datagram)) max-bytes)\n      (deposit-event!\n        deposit\n        (datagram/datagram-event\n          identity\n          (.-address ^io/InternetAddress (.-address datagram))\n          (.-port datagram)\n          (.-data datagram))))))\n\n\n(defn bind!\n  \"Bind one RawDatagramSocket per the seam contract. `:bind-host` is the\n   local interface address (the wildcard address is legal), `:bind-port` 0\n   asks for an ephemeral port, `:max-bytes` defaults to 1200 and is the\n   symmetric datagram budget. Returns {:send! f :close! f} at once, before\n   the asynchronous bind completes: `:send!` is (send! host port bytes) ->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
